    "id": "class-11__algebra__linear-inequalities__graphical-representation",
    "classLevel": "Class 11",
    "chapter": "Algebra",
    "topic": "Linear Inequalities",
    "subtopic": "Graphical representation",
    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">Class 11 / Algebra / Linear Inequalities</p><h2>Graphical representation</h2><p>Graphical representation is a specific idea in Linear Inequalities.</p>\n<p>Graphical representation studies algebraic structure through operations and structure-preserving maps.</p>\n<p>The exact objects and homomorphisms decide which theorem applies.</p>\n<p>It matters because students must know exactly when the method or theorem is valid.</p></section></div>",
