    "simplifiedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"step-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon target\"></span><h3>Step-by-step method</h3></div><ul><li>Construction is best learned through one clear example.</li><li>Name the object, check the condition, apply the rule, and verify the result.</li></ul></section></div>",
    "advancedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"concept-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon sparkles\"></span><h3>Next mathematical idea</h3></div><p>Construction becomes deeper when stated with exact assumptions and counterexamples.</p>\n<p>Advanced mathematics studies which structures preserve the idea and where the rule stops working.</p></section></div>",
