  {
    "sourceRow": 1090,
    "id": "ug-year-1__linear-algebra-i__systems-and-matrices__linear-systems",
    "classLevel": "UG Year 1",
    "chapter": "Linear Algebra I",
    "topic": "Systems and Matrices",
    "subtopic": "Linear systems",
    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">UG Year 1 / Linear Algebra I / Systems and Matrices</p><h2>Linear systems</h2><p>Linear systems explains a specific idea inside Systems and Matrices.</p>\n<p>It shows what the object means, how it is used, and what must be checked before solving.</p>\n<p>This helps students use Linear Algebra I accurately in examples and proofs.</p></section></div>",
    "detailedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"concept-card hero-explanation\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon sparkles\"></span><h3>Learn clearly</h3></div><h2>Linear systems</h2><p>Start with the main idea, then use the examples to check that the idea is clear in your mind.</p></section><section class=\"key-takeaways\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon check-circle\"></span><h3>Key Point</h3></div><p>Linear systems depends on precise definitions and hypotheses.</p></section><section class=\"key-takeaways\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon check-circle\"></span><h3>Key takeaway</h3></div><p>The central idea is <strong>Linear systems</strong>. Say it in your own words before moving to practice.</p></section></div>",
    "realtimeExamples": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"example-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon pencil\"></span><h3>Worked classroom examples</h3></div><ul><li>Example 1 - Easy: For Linear systems, choose a simple value or equation. Work one step at a time, keep both sides balanced, and substitute the answer back to check that the original statement is true.</li><li>Example 2 - Contrast: A similar-looking problem can be wrong if it breaks the condition, unit, order, or definition.</li><li>Example 3 - Application: Use Linear systems with finding an unknown price, comparing mobile plans, balancing scores, or changing a recipe.</li><li>Visual Model: Show the idea using a balance scale, table of values, expression tree, or graph and explain what each part represents.</li></ul></section><section class=\"real-life-connection\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon globe\"></span><h3>Real-life connection</h3></div><p>Linear systems becomes easier when you connect it with objects, quantities, shapes, patterns, or measurements you can actually see.</p></section></div>",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"step-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon target\"></span><h3>Step-by-step method</h3></div><ul><li>Linear systems is like keeping a balance.</li><li>Each step must preserve the same value or relationship, so the final answer still fits the original problem.</li></ul></section></div>",
    "advancedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"concept-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon sparkles\"></span><h3>Next mathematical idea</h3></div><p>Linear systems connects symbols with structure-preserving operations.</p>\n<p>In higher algebra, the same reasoning appears through equations, functions, matrices, rings, vector spaces, or abstract maps.</p></section></div>",
    "practicePrompt": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"practice-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon target\"></span><h3>Quick check</h3></div><ul><li>Create one example for Linear systems.</li><li>Solve it step by step, show a quick check, and explain one common mistake a student might make.</li></ul></section><section class=\"key-takeaways\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon check-circle\"></span><h3>Before you go next</h3></div><ul><li>Can you state the main idea?</li><li>Can you give one example?</li><li>Can you avoid the common mistake?</li></ul></section></div>",
    "updatedAt": 1786273375990
  },
