    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">UG Year 2 / Probability and Statistics / Statistical Inference</p><h2>Maximum likelihood</h2><p>Maximum likelihood explains a specific idea inside Statistical Inference.</p>\n<p>It shows what the object means, how it is used, and what must be checked before solving.</p>\n<p>This helps students use Probability and Statistics accurately in examples and proofs.</p></section></div>",
