    "detailedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"concept-card hero-explanation\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon sparkles\"></span><h3>Learn clearly</h3></div><h2>Ideals and varieties</h2><p>Start with the main idea, then use the examples to check that the idea is clear in your mind.</p></section><section class=\"key-takeaways\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon check-circle\"></span><h3>Key Point</h3></div><p>Ideals and varieties studies algebraic structure through operations and structure-preserving maps.</p>\n<p>The exact objects and homomorphisms decide which theorem applies.</p></section><section class=\"key-takeaways\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon check-circle\"></span><h3>Key takeaway</h3></div><p>The central idea is <strong>Ideals and varieties</strong>. Say it in your own words before moving to practice.</p></section></div>",
    "realtimeExamples": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"example-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon pencil\"></span><h3>Worked classroom examples</h3></div><ul><li>Example 1 - Easy: For Ideals and varieties, use a small group, ring, field, or vector space. State the operation, compute one example, and check the required property.</li><li>Example 2 - Contrast: If the required condition is missing, Ideals and varieties may not apply even when the notation looks similar.</li><li>Example 3 - Application: In Algebraic Geometry, this topic helps decide whether a calculation, model, theorem, or algorithm is valid.</li><li>Visual Model: Use a small diagram, table, graph, or symbolic example that shows the exact object involved in Ideals and varieties.</li></ul></section><section class=\"real-life-connection\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon globe\"></span><h3>Real-life connection</h3></div><p>Ideals and varieties becomes easier when you connect it with objects, quantities, shapes, patterns, or measurements you can actually see.</p></section></div>",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"step-card\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon target\"></span><h3>Step-by-step method</h3></div><ul><li>Ideals and varieties is easiest when you attach it to one small example.</li><li>Name the setting, check the condition, then use the rule only for that setting.</li></ul></section></div>",
