    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">PG / MSc Electives / Algebraic Number Theory / Number Fields</p><h2>Algebraic integers</h2><p>Algebraic integers is a specific idea in Number Fields.</p>\n<p>Algebraic integers is a method or condition for choosing the best feasible option.</p>\n<p>Feasibility, objective function, and assumptions determine the correct result.</p>\n<p>It matters because students must know exactly when the method or theorem is valid.</p></section></div>",
