    "subtopic": "Network flows",
    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">PG / MSc Electives / Graph Theory / Advanced Graph Theory</p><h2>Network flows</h2><p>Network flows is a specific idea in Advanced Graph Theory.</p>\n<p>Network flows studies graph structure or processes on networks.</p>\n<p>The meaning depends on vertices, edges, weights, time, and the question being asked.</p>\n<p>It matters because students must know exactly when the method or theorem is valid.</p></section></div>",
