    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">PG / MSc Electives / Control Theory / Systems and Control</p><h2>Riccati equations</h2><p>Riccati equations is a specific idea in Systems and Control.</p>\n<p>Riccati equations studies algebraic structure through operations and structure-preserving maps.</p>\n<p>The exact objects and homomorphisms decide which theorem applies.</p>\n<p>It matters because students must know exactly when the method or theorem is valid.</p></section></div>",
