    "introduction": "<div class=\"lesson-content\"><section class=\"lesson-introduction\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><span class=\"lesson-icon book-open\"></span><h3>Lesson focus</h3></div><p class=\"eyebrow\">PhD / Research / Applied Mathematics - PDE and Scientific Computing / Nonlinear PDE</p><h2>Reaction-diffusion systems</h2><p>Reaction-diffusion systems is a specific idea in Nonlinear PDE.</p>\n<p>Reaction-diffusion systems uses equations, networks, or stochastic models to represent a biological process.</p>\n<p>The important step is matching variables and assumptions to the real mechanism.</p>\n<p>It matters because students must know exactly when the method or theorem is valid.</p></section></div>",
