    "introduction": "Conjecture formulation is an advanced idea in Research Design and Communication. It gives precise language for a research question, model, proof, or method. Learning it helps students judge claims carefully instead of trusting vague similarity.",
    "detailedExplanation": "Basic Idea: Conjecture formulation turns observed patterns into precise statements that may be proved or disproved.\n\nHow It Works: First state the objects. Next write the assumptions clearly. Then use the principle only when those assumptions are satisfied.\n\nWhy It Works: Research mathematics depends on exact conditions. If a condition is missing, the same method can give a false conclusion.\n\nWhere We Use It: It is used in Research Practice for modelling, algorithms, proofs, communication, or research design.\n\nCommon mistake: Using a powerful idea without checking its definitions, limits, or data assumptions.\n\nCorrect idea: Check the setting, test a small example, and look for a counterexample before generalising.\n\nPrinciple: Conjecture formulation turns observed patterns into precise statements that may be proved or disproved.\n\nWorked Example: Testing examples can suggest a theorem but never proves it.\n\nVerification: Compare with a known simple case, check assumptions, and confirm the conclusion follows.\n\nVisual Understanding: Picture papers, theorem statements, proof maps, examples, and reproducibility checklists. Notice which parts are inputs, rules, outputs, and limitations.\n\nMemory Trick: Use S-A-E: Setting, Assumption, Example.\n\n**Key Point:** Conjecture formulation turns observed patterns into precise statements that may be proved or disproved.",
    "realtimeExamples": "Example 1 - Easy: Testing examples can suggest a theorem but never proves it.\nExample 2 - Counterexample: Change one assumption and ask whether the conclusion still holds. If not, the assumption was essential.\nExample 3 - Application: This idea helps researchers make precise models, proofs, algorithms, or communication choices in Research Design and Communication.\nVisual Model: Use papers, theorem statements, proof maps, examples, and reproducibility checklists to keep the concept concrete before using formal notation.",
    "simplifiedExplanation": "Conjecture formulation is not just a name. Learn the setting, the needed assumption, and one example. That makes the research idea easier to trust and use.",
    "advancedExplanation": "A good conjecture states assumptions, conclusion, and scope. At PhD level, the main skill is knowing the hypotheses, standard examples, limitations, and how the topic connects to nearby research areas.",
    "practicePrompt": "For Conjecture formulation, write the main definition or principle, give one valid example, and explain one limitation or assumption that matters.",
    "updatedAt": 1786245296137
  },
  {
    "sourceRow": 1977,
    "id": "phd-research__research-practice__research-design-and-communication__theorem-proof-development",
